# What the Vercel CLI must not upload.
#
# `vercel deploy` does NOT read .gitignore. Its own default ignore list covers
# .git, node_modules, .next, .vercel and .env.local — but not `.env`, which
# sits right next to them and holds the live database password, AUTH_SECRET,
# the SMTP password and the API keys. A `vercel --prod` from a working
# directory therefore ships the local .env into the build container and into
# the deployment's source listing. Verified with `vercel deploy --dry`, which
# prints exactly which files go up.
#
# Production values come from the project's environment variables, which Vercel
# injects directly; nothing here is needed at build time. prisma.config.ts
# already expects no .env on a host and says so.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Records which Neon org the last `neon` command ran against. Local state.
.neon

# Layout-audit screenshots. Generated, never served.
.shots
